### Timeout and bounded retry (unit 5.6)
### Run two catalog instances: docker compose -f compose.yaml -f compose.labs.yaml up --build -d
### Passwords come from .env.

@gatewayUrl = http://localhost:8080

### 1. Login
# @name userLogin
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "demo-user",
  "password": "<DEMO_USER_PASSWORD from .env>"
}

@userToken = {{userLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### 2. Failover: stop one instance (docker compose -f compose.yaml -f compose.labs.yaml stop catalog-2)
### and send this at once, repeatedly. Expect 200 every time: the retry reaches the other instance.
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/products
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

### 3. Timeout: pause the only catalog instance (docker pause stockflow-catalog).
### Expect 503 problem+json after about 3.4 s (3 attempts of 1 s plus backoff), not a hang.
### Undo with: docker unpause stockflow-catalog
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/products
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
